From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil Reif <pr@sambal.net>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:53:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat: annotate chat images with numbered pins and a
 highlighter
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the image viewer, participants can place numbered map pins and draw
highlighter strokes on any image; tapping an annotation selects it with a
bounding box, dragging moves it and the delete button or key removes it
(own annotations, or any with message.manage). Each annotation is a thread reply to the
image message whose body ends with a marker link
[⌖](#chatto-annot:v1:<assetId>:[mv:<eventId>:]pin|hl:<coords>), so annotations
are shared, live and removable. A move names the annotation it repositions;
the latest move wins. Pins count up in posting order, every annotator gets
their own colour, and the marker link is hidden when messages are rendered.

Server: annotation replies do not auto-follow the thread for the poster or
the image's author, so they cause no thread notifications by themselves.
---
